{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, etc.</b> All the commentators say that this verse concerns the future, and the meaning of the pericope concerns the war of Gog and Magog. Only R. Moses the Kohen says that it is all connected. And after it he says, 'Woe to those who go down to Egypt,' and similarly before it." "And the meaning of <b>the light of the moon</b> is that HaShem will strengthen the light of the moon and the sun after the great rain, and this is a wondrous thing." "<b>Sevenfold.</b> He interpreted it as the prophet interpreted, 'like the light of seven days,' and the meaning is like the light of seven days joined together." "<b>On the day that YHWH binds up.</b> At the time that HaShem heals the blow of Israel in the days of Gog or in the days of Assyria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {3 "Ibn Ezra uses abbreviated forms ירפ׳ and ישר׳; resolved as ירפא and ישראל respectively based on context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:06.907952277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}